nent visa with travel for 5 years from the grant; first entry before the date the Minister sets","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-20","machineReadableUrl":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/F1996B03551/2026-11-03/2026-11-03/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_2/document_2.html"},{"id":"regs-public-interest","url":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/F1996B03551/latest/text/3","title":"Migration Regulations 1994, Schedule 4 Part 1: public interest criteria 4001 to 4005, 4010 and 4015 to 4021","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-20","machineReadableUrl":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/F1996B03551/2026-11-03/2026-11-03/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_3/document_3.html"},{"id":"regs-special-return","url":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/F1996B03551/latest/text/3","title":"Migration Regulations 1994, Schedule 5: special return criteria 5001 (deportation, character cancellation or refusal), 5002 (removal in the last 12 months) and 5010 (sponsored students)","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-20","machineReadableUrl":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/F1996B03551/2026-11-03/2026-11-03/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_3/document_3.html"},{"id":"act-spouse","url":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/C1958A00062/latest/text","title":"Migration Act 1958, sections 5F and 12: a spouse is in a married relationship, under a marriage valid for the Act, which applies Part VA of the Marriage Act 1961 without its section 88E","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-20","machineReadableUrl":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/C1958A00062/2026-10-08/2026-10-08/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_1/document_1.html"},{"id":"act-section-48","url":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/C1958A00062/latest/text","title":"Migration Act 1958, section 48(1) and (1A): a non-citizen in Australia without a substantive visa, refused a visa or with some visas cancelled since last entry, may apply only for prescribed classes","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-20","machineReadableUrl":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/C1958A00062/2026-10-08/2026-10-08/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_1/document_1.html"},{"id":"regs-section-48-classes","url":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/F1996B03551/latest/text","title":"Migration Regulations 1994, regulation 2.12: the visa classes prescribed for section 48 of the Act, which do not include the Skilled—Independent (Permanent) (Class SI) visa","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-20","machineReadableUrl":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/F1996B03551/2026-11-03/2026-11-03/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_1/document_1.html"},{"id":"regs-condition-8515","url":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/F1996B03551/latest/text/3","title":"Migration Regulations 1994, Schedule 8 condition 8515: the holder must not marry or enter into a de facto relationship before entering Australia","kind":"official","verifiedAt":"2026-11-20","machineReadableUrl":"https://www.legislation.gov.au/F1996B03551/2026-11-03/2026-11-03/text/original/epub/OEBPS/document_3/document_3.html"}],"countries":{"id":"countries","number":1},"formerCountries":{"id":"former-countries","number":1},"officialDomains":[{"id":"au","number":1}],"countrySets":[{"id":"au-pacific-regional","number":1}],"requirements":[{"id":"under-45","title":"Under 45: the invitation to apply must come before the 45th birthday","expression":{"op":"lt","left":{"op":"fact","key":"principal.ageYears"},"right":{"op":"int","value":45}},"sources":["regs-1137-invitation"]}],"assessments":[{"id":"invitation","title":"An invitation in writing from the Minister to apply, and an application made within the period it states","evidence":["principal.ageYears"],"sources":["regs-1137-invitation","regs-189-criteria"]},{"id":"skills-assessment","title":"A listed occupation named in the invitation, assessed as suitable by its assessing authority, not for a 485 visa; at invitation within its stated validity of up to 3 years, else at most 3 years old","evidence":["principal.educationLevel"],"sources":["regs-1137-invitation","regs-189-criteria"]},{"id":"registered-course","title":"If the skills assessment rests on a qualification obtained in Australia while holding a student visa, the qualification came from studying a registered course","evidence":["principal.educationLevel"],"sources":["regs-189-criteria"]},{"id":"competent-english","title":"Competent English at the time of invitation: a specified test score from the last 3 years, or a passport of a type the Minister specifies","evidence":["principal.citizenships"],"sources":["regs-189-criteria","regs-competent-english"]},{"id":"points-score","title":"A points-test score at least the score in the invitation and the pass mark, from age, English, work experience, qualifications, the partner''s skills and other attributes","evidence":["principal.ageYears","principal.educationLevel"],"sources":["regs-189-criteria","regs-points-test"]},{"id":"regional-provisional-visa","title":"A principal who holds a subclass 491 or 494 visa, or whose last substantive visa was one, has held it at least 3 years at application, unless the Minister''s instrument excuses it","evidence":["principal.residenceCountry"],"sources":["regs-189-criteria"]},{"id":"where-to-apply","title":"In or outside Australia, not in immigration clearance; in Australia, holding a substantive visa or a Bridging A, B or C visa; a family member applies before the decision on the principal","evidence":["principal.residenceCountry"],"sources":["regs-1137-application"]},{"id":"section-48","title":"In Australia without a substantive visa after a refusal since last entry (not of a bridging visa or on character grounds) or some cancellations: subclass 189 cannot be applied for there (Act s 48)","evidence":["principal.visaRefusals"],"sources":["act-section-48","regs-section-48-classes"]},{"id":"character","title":"The principal and each family member, applying or not, satisfy the character criterion 4001, giving a police statement and form 80 when the Minister asks","evidence":["principal.visaRefusals"],"sources":["regs-189-character","regs-189-secondary","regs-public-interest","regs-character-documents"]},{"id":"security","title":"Principal and each family member, applying or not: no security risk, no foreign policy, weapons or unwaived sanctions bar, no critical technology risk (criteria 4002, 4003, 4003B)","evidence":["principal.citizenships"],"sources":["regs-189-character","regs-189-secondary","regs-public-interest"]},{"id":"commonwealth-debts","title":"The principal and each family member, applying or not, owe no debt to the Commonwealth, unless the Minister is satisfied that arrangements to pay it were made (criterion 4004)","evidence":["unit.liquidAssets"],"sources":["regs-189-character","regs-189-secondary","regs-public-interest"]},{"id":"no-false-information","title":"Criterion 4020: no bogus document or false information on the application or a visa held 12 months before, nor a refusal for it in 3 years (waivable); identity proven, no refusal for it in 10 years","evidence":["principal.visaRefusals"],"sources":["regs-189-character","regs-189-secondary","regs-public-interest"]},{"id":"passport","title":"The principal and each family member applying hold a valid passport issued by an official source, unless it would be unreasonable to require one (criterion 4021)","evidence":["principal.citizenships"],"sources":["regs-189-character","regs-189-secondary","regs-public-interest"]},{"id":"values-statement","title":"The principal and each family member applying who had turned 18 at the time of application sign a values statement, unless compelling circumstances excuse it (criterion 4019)","evidence":["principal.ageYears"],"sources":["regs-189-character","regs-189-secondary","regs-public-interest"]},{"id":"health","title":"The principal and each family member applying meet the health criterion 4005, and so does each family member not applying unless it would be unreasonable to require an assessment","evidence":["principal.ageYears"],"sources":["regs-189-health","regs-189-secondary","regs-public-interest"]},{"id":"establishment","title":"The principal and each family member applying are likely to become established in Australia without undue personal difficulty or undue difficulties or costs to the community (criterion 4010)","evidence":["unit.liquidAssets"],"sources":["regs-189-health","regs-189-secondary","regs-public-interest"]},{"id":"minors","title":"For a family member under 18 applying: the home country''s law permits removal, or each person who can decide where the child lives consents, or a child order fits; and the child''s best interests","evidence":["principal.ageYears"],"sources":["regs-189-character","regs-189-secondary","regs-public-interest"]},{"id":"special-return","title":"Criteria 5001, 5002, 5010: no deportation; no character cancellation or refusal unless cleared as 5001 says; 12 months since a removal under s 198, 199 or 205 unless waived; sponsored students'' terms","evidence":["principal.visaRefusals"],"sources":["regs-189-special-return","regs-189-secondary","regs-special-return"]},{"id":"first-entry","title":"Outside Australia at grant: first entry before the date the Minister sets; a family member may be barred from marrying or entering a de facto relationship before entering (condition 8515)","evidence":["principal.residenceCountry"],"sources":["regs-189-visa-period","regs-condition-8515"]}],"dependents":[{"id":"spouse","title":"Spouse: a marriage valid for the Migration Act (the Marriage Act''s Part VA, s 12) and an exclusive, genuine, continuing shared life (s 5F); a recorded marriage is read as meeting it","path":["spouse"],"condition":{"op":"bool","value":true},"sources":["regs-family-unit","act-spouse","regs-189-secondary"]},{"id":"partner","title":"De facto partner aged 18 or more, together for at least 12 months (a shorter relationship that is registered, or with compelling reasons: possible)","path":["partner"],"condition":{"op":"all","operands":[{"op":"gte","left":{"op":"fact","key":"p